# Rust / Tauri
/src-tauri/target/
/src-tauri/gen/
**/*.rs.bk

# Node
node_modules/
dist/
dist-ssr/
.vite/
*.local

# Secrets — nothing here ever gets committed
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
canvas_token*

# Local data — contains my actual grades
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
/data/
*.ics

# Degree records. A real MyProgress export is a full academic transcript —
# student id, every grade, every attempt. The committed test fixture is
# synthetic (tests/fixtures/myprogress_sample.txt) precisely so this rule can
# stay absolute. Drop a real export at the path below to have degree_test
# verify the parser against it; it never leaves your machine.
/src-tauri/tests/fixtures/myprogress_real.txt
*MyProgress*.pdf
*My Progress*.pdf

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.swp

# Build artifacts
/src-tauri/Cargo.lock.orig
*.log

# ── Additions beyond SPEC.md §12 ────────────────────────────────────────────
# The spec's list assumes macOS. This repo is developed cross-platform, and a
# few things it does not mention are worth keeping out of history.

# Windows shell debris (Thumbs.db above is only half of it)
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# Linux
.directory
*~

# The harvested Canvas session lives in the OS credential store, but the
# documented fallback in §1 is a 0600 file in the app config dir. If that path
# is ever pointed at the repo during debugging, this is the backstop.
session.json
cookies.json
/src-tauri/.session*

# sqlx offline query cache is intentionally NOT ignored — it must be committed
# so the project builds without a live database. See docs/DEVELOPMENT.md.
# (no entry for /src-tauri/.sqlx/ on purpose)

# TypeScript build info
*.tsbuildinfo

# Test and coverage output
/coverage/
